.SH ENVIRONMENT
Every configuration key can be overridden by an environment variable named
.BI MU2E_POWER_RECOVERY_ KEY
with the dotted path upper-cased and dots replaced by underscores, for example
.B MU2E_POWER_RECOVERY_SSH_CONNECT_TIMEOUT
for
.IR ssh.connect_timeout .
.B VAULT_ADDR
and
.B VAULT_TOKEN
are honoured in their conventional form.
.PP
Priority, lowest first: built-in defaults, the YAML config file,
.IR config/.env ,
the environment, the command line.
.PP
Three further variables are read directly rather than as configuration keys:
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set to any non-empty value, output is not coloured, whatever the terminal
is.
.TP
.B FORCE_COLOR
When set, output is coloured even when stdout is not a terminal \(em for
capturing a coloured transcript into a file or a pipe.
.B NO_COLOR
wins if both are set.
.TP
.B MU2E_POWER_RECOVERY_UPDATED
Set to
.B 1
by phase 0 across its re-execution, so the new process does not check for
updates again. It exists to make an update loop impossible and is not intended
to be set by hand. Setting it does skip the check, like
.BR \-\-no\-self\-update ,
but the run reports it as having already updated rather than as disabled.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every phase completed and nothing failed.
.TP
.B 1
A phase completed but one or more nodes failed their checks.
.TP
.B 2
The run could not start: configuration, credentials, or no reachable gateway.
.TP
.B 3
Interrupted by the operator.
.SH EXAMPLES
Read-only survey of the configured locations:
.PP
.RS
.EX
mu2e-power-recovery \-\-phase assess
.EE
.RE
.PP
Rehearse the whole four-phase run with no cluster attached:
.PP
.RS
.EX
mu2e-power-recovery \-\-phase all \-\-simulate
.EE
.RE
.PP
A real recovery, with a root principal and a label for the logbook:
.PP
.RS
.EX
mu2e-power-recovery \-\-phase all \-\-execute \e
    \-\-principal anorman@FNAL.GOV \e
    \-\-root\-principal anorman/root@FNAL.GOV \e
    \-\-label "Sept 2026 planned outage"
.EE
.RE
.PP
Resume a power-on that stopped at the
.I dcs
stage, after fixing it:
.PP
.RS
.EX
mu2e-power\-on \-\-execute \-\-from dcs
.EE
.RE
.PP
Regenerate and post the report for an earlier run:
.PP
.RS
.EX
mu2e-power\-report \-\-run\-id 17 \-\-post\-ecl
.EE
.RE
